    feat(offshore): native remote-dispatch tool family + /offshore TUI toggle

    OffshoreProvider (crates/ocean-runtime/src/tools/offshore/) gives every Ocean
    assistant ten offshore_* tools to run agent work on a REMOTE Ocean daemon in
    per-job git worktrees and ship results back over git: health, workspace,
    dispatch, sessions, events, cancel, ship, fetch, clean, mode. Registered from
    the [offshore] table in ocean.toml (remote_url, ssh_host, ssh_bin,
    remote_root, turn_timeout_secs, enabled) — absent/disabled config registers
    nothing, zero behavior change.

    Ported 1:1 from the battle-tested ocean-agents offshore CLI, encoding its
    hard-won lessons: mirror clones push by URL with explicit refspecs (mirror
    remotes reject per-branch pushes), mirror refresh fetches heads-only with no
    prune (prune would delete live job branches), dispatch waits out synchronous
    remote turns (default 900s), SSE is live-only and timeout-bounded, remote cwd
    is never validated so tools steer the model to workspace-returned cwds only.
    Hardened beyond the reference: charset-validated job/repo names, shell-quoted
    refs and URLs, bounded ssh/git execution, capped events output.

    The TUI grows /offshore [on|off|status] — a persistent toggle at
    ~/.config/offshore/mode (shared with the CLI's 'mode' subcommand). While ON,
    both turn-submission paths (legacy TUI and shell) fill AgentTurnRequest
    .guidance steering heavy/subagent work through the offshore_* tools.

    Tests: 26 offshore unit tests (script assembly pins both git fixes), config
    parse + registry gating tests, /offshore slash + guidance tests; also fixes
    two pre-existing test races (kitty temp-PNG path, HOME-mutating tests) that
    made the ocean-tui suite flaky under the parallel runner.

